// Run only in the new PoC LAW after AuditEvent is enabled and data arrives.
// Results contain sensitive identities and addresses: keep them in ignored local evidence.
// Column names confirmed against real AZKVAuditLogs output on 2026-10-18.
//
// IMPORTANT: ResultType can read "Success" for a request that was DENIED. Always read HttpStatusCode,
// ResultSignature (for example 403 / Forbidden) and ResultDescription (the denial reason).
AZKVAuditLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(24h)
| project TimeGenerated, OperationName, ResultType, ResultSignature, HttpStatusCode, ResultDescription,
          CallerIpAddress, Identity, TrustedService, IsAddressAuthorized, IsRbacAuthorized,
          ClientInfo, RequestUri, CorrelationId
| order by TimeGenerated asc
// Inspect all operations first, including failures and administrative calls.
// TrustedService shows which trusted-service category the vault assigned to the caller (for example
// AzureDatabricks). A caller address alone is not proof of the network path.